  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "The paper on which you are reading this text is approximately $0.0001$ metres thick.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p27-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "How thick would the paper be if it were folded 10 times? Please calculate the result, but do not attempt it.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$10.24\\text{ cm}$",
          "worked": "Each fold doubles the thickness. After $n$ folds, the thickness is $h(n)=0.0001\\times2^n$ metres.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}h(10)&=0.0001\\times2^{10}\\\\h(10)&=0.1024\\text{ m}\\\\h(10)&=10.24\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many times would you have to fold this paper so that the paper is thick enough to reach the moon? Note: The moon is $384\\,400\\,000$ metres away.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p27-q13-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "42 times.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p27-q13-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Solve ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "0.0001\\times2^n=384\\,400\\,000",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " using logarithms, then take the next whole number of folds.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Each fold doubles the thickness. Find the threshold number of folds:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}0.0001\\times2^n&=384\\,400\\,000\\\\2^n&=3\\,844\\,000\\,000\\,000\\\\\\log_{10}(2^n)&=\\log_{10}(3\\,844\\,000\\,000\\,000)\\\\n\\log_{10}2&=\\log_{10}(3\\,844\\,000\\,000\\,000)\\\\n&=\\frac{\\log_{10}(3\\,844\\,000\\,000\\,000)}{\\log_{10}2}\\\\n&\\approx41.81\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe number of folds must be a whole number and the thickness must reach the moon, so at least 42 folds are required.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
